  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It should be a no brainer to anyone who has played the game that despite VRC itself only being under 1GB in size, downloading worlds and avatars can take up a lot of space on someone's hard drive who might not have/want to use all that space at once, while at the same time the current limit of 20GB for cached data can be limiting if you do have a large drive and don't want to redownload a world that you have already been to.\nA solution to this can be something that PlayStation Home did back while it was still an active service, where it allowed users to manually adjust how much of their hard drive should be dedicated to PSHome downloads, from only a few Gbs to their entire drive if they really wanted to, the same system could be implemented to VRC to give those with smaller drives a better experience accessing the few worlds they visit, or give an extra boost to people like me who tend to world hop often and don't want to redownload an entire world again when showing my friends around. The standard 20GB limit can of course stay as a 'default option' too.",
